  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance floor. Config_001 (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA-2000) is the simplest, most standard baseline in the design space. It tests how much signal RNA alone provides with a straightforward linear dimensionality reduction, giving a reference point against which to measure the incremental value of (a) image modality, (b) learned RNA encoders (scvi, scGPT), (c) multiprofile aggregation, and (d) multimodal fusion. Establishing this floor first ensures that in the remaining 9 experiments I can make informed exploitation/exploration trade-offs rather than assuming complexity will help. It is also the lowest-cost configuration to run, allowing a quick readout to guide the next step."
